+    --keyboard-to-touch=...
+        Maps a key on the keyboard to a point on the simulated touch screen of
+        the device. Pressing the key will behave like touching that part of the
+        screen.
+
+        This is three parts separated by commas: the name of a key (as reported
+        by SDL2, e.g. Space, Return, Left, Right, A, B, 1, 2), the X co-ordinate
+        and the Y co-ordinate.
+        The co-ordinates are floating-point (decimal) numbers. 0,0 is the
+        top-left corner. The bottom-right corner is 320,480 if the app is in
+        portrait, and 480,320 if the app is in landscape.
+
+        For example, --keyboard-to-touch=Space,470,310 will make the space bar
+        simulate tapping in the bottom-right corner of the screen, for a
+        landscape game.
+
+        Multiple keys can be mapped by passing this option more than once, and
+        several mapped keys may be held simultaneously. This is not used by
+        default.
+
